<title>UK: NWE naphtha pressured by crude, supplies.</title>
<headline>NWE naphtha pressured by crude, supplies.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>NWE naphtha was weak again on Wednesday, under pressure from declining values in crude oil, continued offers in NWE and poor demand.</p>
<p>Dealers said the market had possibly slipped a little from the $173.50 cif NWE paid by an end user on Tuesday for a paraffinic cargo, and the pressure was being kept up by a Moroccan cargo which remained unsold.</p>
<p>N+A material remains unwanted as gasoline remains very depressed.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
